From: Hermes Agent (smolVLM vision server setup)
Date: 2026-05-24
Subject: Fix SmolVLM IDEfics3 token lookup — remove <global-img> from start marker

SmolVLM's GGUF from ggml-org/SmolVLM-Instruct-GGUF doesn't include the
`<global-img>` special token in its vocabulary. The llama.cpp IDEfics3
multimodal projector code tries to look up this token at initialization,
gets LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL back, and stores it in the overview image start
token vector. When an image is processed, the null token is pushed into
the server token stream, throwing "Invalid token" 400 errors.

Fix: remove `<global-img>` from the fallback chain. The remaining token
`<fake_token_around_image>` exists in the vocabulary (token ID 49152)
and is sufficient for correct image boundary marking.

Upstream PR reference: (not yet submitted)

--- a/tools/mtmd/mtmd.cpp
+++ b/tools/mtmd/mtmd.cpp
@@ -369,7 +369,7 @@
                 {
                     // https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/a42ba80fa520c784c8f11a973ca9034e5f859b79/src/transformers/models/idefics3/processing_idefics3.py#L192-L215
                     slice_tmpl         = MTMD_SLICE_TMPL_IDEFICS3;
-                    tok_ov_img_start   = {lookup_token("\n\n"), lookup_token("<fake_token_around_image>"), lookup_token("<global-img>")};
+                    tok_ov_img_start   = {lookup_token("<fake_token_around_image>")};
                     tok_ov_img_end     = {lookup_token("<fake_token_around_image>")};
                     tok_row_end        = {lookup_token("\n")};
                     sli_img_start_tmpl = "<fake_token_around_image><row_%d_col_%d>";
